# Characterization performance benchmarks — timing-dependent, never sealed.
# (The golden corpus under tests/golden IS committed; perf results are not.)
tests/perf_results/

# SQL read-matrix harness output. Every run regenerates it, and the raw
# payloads are ~159 MB across ~11k files — too much to carry in history for a
# public repo. What the issue write-ups actually cite is kept: the reports, the
# per-case failure records, and the dataset/fixture manifests needed to read
# them. Regenerate the rest with `python -m scripts.sql_read_matrix`.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `audit/` ignore: audit/AUDIT_*.md and
# audit/detail/*.md are hand-written and tracked, and a blanket rule would also
# swallow future ones.
# ``**`` rather than a single level: a run nests copies of these under
# runs/ and historical_original_expectations/, and an anchored pattern misses
# them — which is how 108 KB of nested payload reached the first commit.
audit/sql_read_matrix*/**/runs/
audit/sql_read_matrix*/runs/
audit/sql_read_matrix*/**/results.json
audit/sql_read_matrix*/**/expectations.json
audit/sql_read_matrix*/**/original_expectations.json
audit/sql_read_matrix*/**/case_results.csv
audit/sql_read_matrix*/results.json
audit/sql_read_matrix*/expectations.json
audit/sql_read_matrix*/original_expectations.json
audit/sql_read_matrix*/case_results.csv
